en it  came to the Vatican Bank because every  other Pope has said the right things  when they became Pope about reforming  the bank and they failed to do so so  when he became Pope Peter in 2013 and he  said I'm going to reform the bank I'm  more or less said to Tricia oh sure I've  heard that before but but he changed my  mind in the following way  first of all whoever is Pope today they  would have to be reforming the bank and  the reason for that is it's a quirk of  finances but in 99 Italy decided to go  with the euro when it did that meant the  Vatican was in a quandary because they  used the Italian lira for their own  currency so they had to decide whether  they wanted to print their own currency  or go with the euro so they decided to  go with the euro they didn't know when  they went with the euro that meant that  Brussels wanted some oversight on their  central reserved their Vatican Bank so  as a result of Brussels coming in they  the Vatican have had to pass their  first-ever law against the financing of  terrorism in 2011 their first-ever law  against money laundering in 2011 they  never had a law against money laundering  there  first ever law against how much money  you could bring in undisclosed into the  Vatican so they had to come somewhat  compliant by the European standards but  Francis has done it with enthusiasm and  vigor what I mean by that is he's  brought in independent outsiders layman  who are in fact really trying to change  the culture of no transparency and make  it a compliant bank moving forward in  the 21st century he may succeed he needs  to be Pope for another three to five  years to have the it take effect all the  way down the bureaucracy what is the  official name of this bank the the  Institute for the works of religion  Institute opera opera religion and then  I always love that that the Institute  for the works of religion is the Vatican  Bank so sometimes the don't go always by  the name of the institution look behind  the